50f203fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713860} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fe1478f-929c-5251-9513-40a891596c66" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\mathbf{a}_{2}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713877} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a12d975c-df88-51fc-a7f2-f03198d929a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713879} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf49434-9ea8-5034-8de7-5559302ef240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a12d975c-df88-51fc-a7f2-f03198d929a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713879} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3fc7ec9-7ace-5d70-b56f-8d9a5d3af484" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c4c57ef2-a34c-5daa-84ae-93329e90e32d" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind bases of $S=\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$ by inspection. **Select every set that is a basis of $S$.**" :question/worked-solution "A **basis** must be linearly independent and span $S$.\n\nIf $\\mathbf{a}_{3}=t\\mathbf{a}_{1}$, coordinate $1$ would force $t=1$. But coordinate $2$ would then give $(1)(0)=0\\ne 1$. Thus these two nonzero vectors are not parallel and are linearly independent.\n\nTo have $\\mathbf{a}_{2}=x\\mathbf{a}_{1}+y\\mathbf{a}_{3}$, coordinates $3$ and $2$ force $x=2$ and $y=0$. The remaining coordinate would have to be $(2)(1)+(0)(1)=2$; the displayed value is $2$.\n\nChecking the proposed combination gives\n\n$$\n(2)\\mathbf{a}_{1}+(0)\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{a}_{2}.\n$$\n\nRemoving $\\mathbf{a}_{2}$ leaves the span unchanged. The parallel pair $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1},\\mathbf{a}_{2}\\}$ is dependent. Pairing either nonzero vector on that line with $\\mathbf{a}_{3}$ gives an independent spanning pair. No singleton spans the two independent directions, and the triple is dependent.\n\nTherefore, select exactly these bases:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathcal{B}_{1}&=\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1},\\mathbf{a}_{3}\\} \\\\ \\mathcal{B}_{2}&=\\{\\mathbf{a}_{2},\\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15227513-3e10-577d-8b73-986efde25d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713828} {:answer/id #uuid "5234acfd-49b2-5441-920b-6b01f184060f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15227513-3e10-577d-8b73-986efde25d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713828} :answer-field/id #uuid "158b62e0-7bf1-5b62-a1a4-c55ad9f0e380" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\mathbf{a}_{2}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a4656e3-8fff-5a37-a93c-241a49465f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713876} {:answer/id #uuid "a10f3a6a-f95f-5