ty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b86b782a-b2fe-5ac0-bbd3-f9f70a04c59e" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a_{1} &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad a_{2} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ a_{3} &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad a_{4} &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a basis $B$ of $S=\\operatorname{Span}\\{a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{4}\\}$ by identifying pivot columns." :question/worked-solution "Place the vectors in the columns of a matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}+2R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{3}\\leftarrow R_{3}+R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{4}\\leftarrow R_{4}+R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{3}\\leftarrow R_{3}+2R_{2}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{4}\\leftarrow R_{4}-2R_{2}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe leading nonzero entries are in columns $1, 2$. Select the corresponding columns from the **original matrix**, giving $B=\\{a_{1},\\;a_{2}\\}$:\n\n$$\nB=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThese pivot columns are linearly independent and span the column space of $A$, which is $S$. The nonpivot columns can be removed without changing the span. Row operations locate the pivot indices; use the original vectors when writing the basis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "562097be-0d00-5c2d-a634-e3131493fbb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714094} {:answer/id #uuid "6603df77-becc-5827-bd30-af1101d14379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714097} {:answer/id #uuid "81a6156a-5b0b-5130-8a61-a51f21037041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714101} {:answer/id #uuid "bd726dcb-a8bf-5946-871f-9713eec2cea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714108} {:answer/id #uuid "d2020c9b-40f3-574a-b753-be6a8b208c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6603df77-becc-5827-bd30-af1101d14379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714097} :answer-field/id #uuid "351f8c7d-2914-5ae2-8ca8-34de41131a71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bb5a602d-bcc0-53ef-9878-b493da1f91f2" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a_{1} &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad a_{2} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ a_{3} &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad a_{4} &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a basis $B$ of $S=\\operatorname{Span}\\{a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{4}\\}$ by identifying pivot columns." :question/worked-solution "Place the vectors in the columns of a matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}+2R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{3}\\leftarrow R_{3}-R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{4}\\leftarrow R_{4}+R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{3}\\leftarrow R_{3}+R_{2}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{4}\\leftarrow R_{4}-R_{2}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{4}\\leftarrow R_{4}-R_{3}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe leading nonzero entries are in columns $1, 3, 4$. Select the corresponding columns from the **original matrix**, giving $B=\\{a_{1},\\;a_{3},\\;a_{4}\\}$:\n\n$$\nB=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThese pivot columns are linearly independent and span the column space of $A$, which is $S$. The nonpivot columns can be removed without changing the span. Row operations locate the pivot indices; use the original vectors when writing the basis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "676e3373-acb7-53a5-b78d-7162059b25fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714098} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac15af0-0457-576a-b7e0-b7977c81e8fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714100} {:answer/id #uuid "cddc5de9-2aea-53d2-ab9a-4039e126ce2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714109} {:answer/id #uuid "cf3d7e7f-79e3-584e-a5a3-9363a36cdd00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714110} {:answer/id #uuid "e51aa1f3-ecc5-5a21-a908-ce06bf2b969a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ac15af0-0457-576a-b7e0-b7977c81e8fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714100} :answer-field/id #uuid "b00ab346-ce8e-5fee-aefb-8084b35e4e86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f85e1c28-55bd-5c5a-b5c5-f5049e615041" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a_{1} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad a_{2} &=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ a_{3} &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad a_{4} &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a basis $B$ of $S=\\operatorname{Span}\\{a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{4}\\}$ by identifying pivot columns." :question/worked-solution "Place the vectors in the columns of a matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}+R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{3}\\leftarrow R_{3}-2R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{4}\\leftarrow R_{4}-2R_{1}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{3}\\leftarrow R_{3}+R_{2}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nApply $R_{4}\\leftarrow R_{4}-R_{2}$:\n\n$$\nA\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe leading nonzero entries are in columns $1, 3$. Select the corresponding columns from the **original matrix**, giving $B=\\{a_{1},\\;a_{3}\\}$:\n\n$$\nB=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThese pivot columns are linearly independent and span the column space of $A$, which is $S$. The nonpivot columns can be removed without changing the span. Row operations locate the pivot indices; use the original vectors when writing the basis."}]}
